	### One entry of Colony Modules' queue (colony modules design § 5): its place,
	### the world and the module (custom loc sr_mq_<n>_world_name and
	### sr_mq_<n>_module_name, from the place's sr_mq_<n>_site and _type), a
	### button that moves it up a place, or to the top on alt-click, as the base
	### game's ship construction queue does (sr_colony_module_queue_up_sgui,
	### scope:op = the place, or the place + 20; hidden on place 1, its cell kept),
	### and a button that removes it (sr_colony_module_queue_sgui, scope:op = the
	### place). Fabrication builds place 1 next. 30 + 200 + 176 + 24 + 24 + 4 × 4
	### spacing + 2 × 4 margin = 478, in the 480 column. Instances in te_sr_mq_rows
	### (sr_sites_generated_rows.gui).
	type te_sr_mq_row = flowcontainer {
